<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Kloof Dec qtr pre-capex net profit rises.</title>
<headline>Kloof Dec qtr pre-capex net profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Quarter to end-Dec versus preceding quarter</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit before capital spending   114.52 vs 93.99</p>
<p>    Capital spending			    78.31 vs 66.85</p>
<p>Full name: Kloof Gold Mining Co Ltd, managed by Gold Fields of South Africa Ltd  </p>
<p>Gold output (kg)</p>
<p>    Kloof-				   5,513.0 vs 5,753.0</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-			     1,918.0 vs 1,447.1</p>
<p>    Libanon-				 2,415.7 vs 2,028.5</p>
<p>Tonnes milled/treated</p>
<p>    Kloof-				  500,000  vs 481,000</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-			    300,000  vs 286,000</p>
<p>    Libanon-				424,000  vs 408,000</p>
<p>Yield (gram/t)</p>
<p>    Kloof-					11.0 vs 12.0</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-				   6.4 vs  5.1</p>
<p>    Libanon-				     5.7 vs  5.0</p>
<p>Cost (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    Kloof-				   38,810  vs 35,421</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-			     52,313  vs 66,383</p>
<p>    Libanon-				 49,704  vs 57,713</p>
<p>Revenue (rand/kg)</p>
<p>    Kloof-				   56,258  vs 55,441</p>
<p>    Leeudoorn-			     56,303  vs 55,324</p>
<p>    Libanon-				 56,325  vs 55,401</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said the effects of production interruptions as a result of the Christmas and New Year holidays are to be reflected in the ensuing quarter.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
